From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:58:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hw/pci-host/ppce500: migrate the host bridge's config space

The e500 host bridge's PCI function (e500-host-bridge) has no vmsd, so
its config space is not migrated. Its BAR0 maps CCSR into PCI memory,
which is where devices' MSI writes reach the MPIC's MSI registers
(MSIIR). After any load BAR0 is unassigned (info pci: "not mapped"),
every MSI is dropped, and a guest whose devices use MSI or MSI-X waits
forever for their interrupts.

Repro: boot Linux on ppce500 with a virtio-blk-pci disk mounted (Linux
gives it MSI-X), savevm, loadvm (in the same process or with -loadvm,
the latter also needing the previous patch), then write a file to the
disk: the guest idles forever with the request completed and its
interrupt lost.

Give the bridge a vmsd with its PCI device state. A snapshot from an
unfixed build still loads (the bridge keeps its reset state, as
before); an unfixed build refuses a new snapshot (unknown section
e500-host-bridge).

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

Origin: new
---
 hw/pci-host/ppce500.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/pci-host/ppce500.c b/hw/pci-host/ppce500.c
index b74b2649e8d5c4ec0627214ca57a211402b63c36..85c5fedb9dafcb24bd9ae315e98506255c36ccae 100644
--- a/hw/pci-host/ppce500.c
+++ b/hw/pci-host/ppce500.c
@@ -509,6 +509,21 @@ static void e500_pcihost_realize(DeviceState *dev, Error **errp)
     pci_bus_set_route_irq_fn(b, e500_route_intx_pin_to_irq);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The bridge's config space: BAR0 maps CCSR into PCI memory, where devices' MSI writes reach the
+ * interrupt controller's MSI registers. Without it a loaded guest's BAR0 is unassigned and every
+ * MSI is lost.
+ */
+static const VMStateDescription vmstate_e500_host_bridge = {
+    .name = "e500-host-bridge",
+    .version_id = 1,
+    .minimum_version_id = 1,
+    .fields = (const VMStateField[]) {
+        VMSTATE_PCI_DEVICE(parent, PPCE500PCIBridgeState),
+        VMSTATE_END_OF_LIST()
+    }
+};
+
 static void e500_host_bridge_class_init(ObjectClass *klass, const void *data)
 {
     DeviceClass *dc = DEVICE_CLASS(klass);
@@ -519,6 +534,7 @@ static void e500_host_bridge_class_init(ObjectClass *klass, const void *data)
     k->device_id = PCI_DEVICE_ID_MPC8533E;
     k->class_id = PCI_CLASS_PROCESSOR_POWERPC;
     dc->desc = "Host bridge";
+    dc->vmsd = &vmstate_e500_host_bridge;
     /*
      * PCI-facing part of the host bridge, not usable without the
      * host-facing part, which can't be device_add'ed, yet.
